  Repaint this grey block mockup as a finished video game screenshot of a cathedral square in a medieval city. 16-bit SNES pixel art, isometric 2:1 projection, warm earthy palette (browns, tans, terracotta, forest green, stone grey, gold, deep red, sky blue), single dark outline, medium shading, light from the top left, medieval central European, 14th century. Crisp pixels, no blur, no text, no UI. Keep EXACTLY the camera, the position, footprint and height of every building, the streets, the water and the little people: the people are 1.7 m tall adults and set the scale; do not shrink or enlarge any building. The huge grey building is a gothic cathedral: two west towers with tall slate spires, a high nave with flying buttresses and pointed stained glass windows, a transept, a rose window; the cream blocks around are half-timbered town houses of 2 and 3 storeys with terracotta and slate roofs. The cobbled square has market stalls, a well, pigeons and many townsfolk. The cathedral must stay exactly as tall as in the mockup relative to the houses and the people.

